# tasks_map_ranges: Map and unmap ranges, valid and not. In the blocks setup a map walks the page table and calls the host's map_memory, and refuses a misaligned offset or length, a zero length, a range beyond the task or one that overflows; in the map and isolate setups a map is a no-op that always completes. An unmap checks the range against the task in-process (blocks and map fault), the range tracker refuses misaligned and empty ranges (blocks only), and the service does no check at all. An unknown task ID faults in every setup ("Invalid task").
